In .NET MAUI, use the **lifecycle events** API in your `MauiProgram.cs` (or app builder configuration):

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is paused
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is stopped
        }));
#elif IOS
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(application =>
        {
            // runs when the app enters background
        }));
#endif
});
```

You'll need `using Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents;` and the platform-specific namespaces (`Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents` covers both).

This approach lets you tap into native lifecycle callbacks without subclassing platform classes directly.
